{"name":"Damascene","hex":"#996d32","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Damascene","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to Damascus.","Pertaining to a sudden and complete change in one's beliefs."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of Damascus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Damascene"}],"entries":[{"title":"Damascus","blocks":[{"text":"Damascus is the capital and largest city of Syria. It is the oldest capital city in the world. Known colloquially in Syria as aš-Šām and dubbed, poetically, the \"City of Jasmine\", Damascus is a major cultural center of the Levant and the Arab world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Damascus%2C_Syria%2C_Panoramic_view_of_Damascus.jpg/330px-Damascus%2C_Syria%2C_Panoramic_view_of_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Damascus","wikidata":"Q3766"},{"title":"Damascena","blocks":[{"text":"Damascena or Damascene was the ancient term for the territory surrounding the city of Damascus in Hellenistic, Roman and Byzantine Syria. Although never a formal province, Damascena was frequently mentioned in Greek and Latin sources. The territory corresponds roughly to the modern Rif Dimashq Governorate of Syria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Description_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale_de_la_Syrie.jpg/330px-Description_g%C3%A9n%C3%A9rale_de_la_Syrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Damascena","wikidata":"Q136687084"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Umayyad_Square%2C_Damascus.jpg/500px-Umayyad_Square%2C_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Umayyad_Square%2C_Damascus.jpg/1280px-Umayyad_Square%2C_Da